{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 84, :comments ["<b>On the day he was anointed.</b> On that very day that he was anointed he offered. And how do I fulfill ״after he was anointed״ (verse 48)? That he was anointed first and then offered — or ״after he was anointed״ means after some time, and it does not come to teach ״on the day he was anointed״ but only to say that he was anointed by day? When it says (Leviticus 7) ״on the day of their anointing,״ we learn that he was anointed by day — so what does ״on the day he was anointed״ teach? On the day he was anointed he offered (Sifrei):" "<b>Twelve silver bowls.</b> They are the very same ones that they donated, and no disqualification occurred in them (there):"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:52.529994222Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}